From 0b2bf3918b23371616156ecf182f3d6396f0b530 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dong Chenchen <superdcc97@163.com>
Date: Wed, 13 May 2026 22:06:44 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 30/30] exit: arbitrate reparented zombie autoreap

Adapted from linux 7.0-rc1 patch to OLK-6.6.
- Use READ_ONCE(p->exit_state) instead of direct access
- Use cmpxchg for ZOMBIE -> DEAD transition in reparent_leader
- Prevents race between reparenting and wait_task_zombie() after
tasklist_lock removal from exit_notify path.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 kernel/exit.c              | 16 +++++---
 opt-patches/report-0028.md | 75 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 85 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 opt-patches/report-0028.md

diff --git a/kernel/exit.c b/kernel/exit.c
index 7649f8667bc7..dd76a874dc79 100644
--- a/kernel/exit.c
+++ b/kernel/exit.c
@@ -696,19 +696,23 @@ static struct task_struct *find_new_reaper(struct task_struct *father,
 static void reparent_leader(struct task_struct *father, struct task_struct *p,
 				struct list_head *dead)
 {
-	if (unlikely(p->exit_state == EXIT_DEAD))
+	if (unlikely(READ_ONCE(p->exit_state) == EXIT_DEAD))
 		return;
 
 	/* We don't want people slaying init. */
 	p->exit_signal = SIGCHLD;
 
-	/* If it has exited notify the new parent about this child's death. */
+	/*
+	 * If it has exited, notify the new parent about this child's death.
+	 * tasklist_lock no longer serializes this path against wait_task_zombie(),
+	 * so arbitrate the ZOMBIE -> DEAD transition the same way as exit_notify().
+	 */
 	if (!p->ptrace &&
-	    p->exit_state == EXIT_ZOMBIE && thread_group_empty(p)) {
-		if (do_notify_parent(p, p->exit_signal)) {
-			p->exit_state = EXIT_DEAD;
+	    READ_ONCE(p->exit_state) == EXIT_ZOMBIE && thread_group_empty(p)) {
+		if (do_notify_parent(p, p->exit_signal) &&
+		    cmpxchg(&p->exit_state, EXIT_ZOMBIE, EXIT_DEAD) ==
+			    EXIT_ZOMBIE)
 			list_add(&p->ptrace_entry, dead);
-		}
 	}
 
 	kill_orphaned_pgrp(p, father);
diff --git a/opt-patches/report-0028.md b/opt-patches/report-0028.md
new file mode 100644
index 000000000000..7073be4585db
--- /dev/null
+++ b/opt-patches/report-0028.md
@@ -0,0 +1,75 @@
+# Patch 0028 Adaptation Report: mm: shard file i_mmap trees by NUMA domain
+
+## Patch Info
+- **Original**: 0028-mm-shard-file-i_mmap-trees-by-NUMA-domain.patch (linux 7.0-rc1)
+- **Status**: Adapted and tested successfully
+- **Commit**: e59c3c774269
+
+## Files Modified
+- `fs/inode.c` — init/cleanup of i_mmap_shards on address_space
+- `include/linux/fs.h` — Added `i_mmap_shard`, `i_mmap_shards` structs; `i_mmap_shards`, `i_mmap_count` fields to `address_space`; updated `mapping_mapped()`
+- `include/linux/mm_types.h` — Added `i_mmap_domain_nid` to `mm_struct`
+- `kernel/fork.c` — Added `task_domain_select_nid()`; set `mm->i_mmap_domain_nid`; updated `file_vma_link_batch_flush` for sharding
+- `mm/Kconfig` — Added `CONFIG_NUMA_DOMAIN_I_MMAP_SHARDS`
+- `mm/internal.h` — Added all i_mmap sharding API declarations and inline stubs
+- `mm/mmap.c` — Added shard allocation, locking, insertion/removal implementations; modified `__vma_link_file`, `__remove_shared_vm_struct`, `vma_prepare`, `vma_complete`, `vma_link_file`, `unlink_file_vma_batch_*`, `vm_lock_mapping`, `vm_unlock_mapping`
+- `mm/khugepaged.c` — Modified `retract_page_tables`, `collapse_file` to iterate sharded roots
+- `mm/memory-failure.c` — Modified `collect_procs_file`, `collect_procs_fsdax` to iterate sharded roots
+- `mm/memory.c` — Modified `unmap_mapping_folio`, `unmap_mapping_pages` to iterate sharded roots
+- `mm/pagewalk.c` — Modified `walk_page_mapping` to iterate sharded roots
+- `mm/rmap.c` — Modified `rmap_walk_file` to iterate sharded roots
+
+## Major Adaptation Conflicts & Resolutions
+
+### 1. mm/vma.c and mm/vma.h don't exist in 6.6
+**Conflict**: In 7.0-rc1, patch adds code to `mm/vma.c` and declarations to `mm/vma.h`. In 6.6, these functions are in `mm/mmap.c` and declarations are in `mm/internal.h`.
+**Resolution**: Put all implementations in `mm/mmap.c` and declarations in `mm/internal.h`.
+
+### 2. kernel/fork.c needs mm/internal.h
+**Conflict**: `kernel/fork.c` calls `i_mmap_*` APIs but doesn't include any mm internal header.
+**Resolution**: Added `#include "../mm/internal.h"` to `kernel/fork.c`.
+
+### 3. file_vma_link_batch_flush location
+**Conflict**: In 7.0-rc1 patch 0025, this function is in `mm/mmap.c`. In 6.6, it's in `kernel/fork.c`.
+**Resolution**: Applied sharding changes to `kernel/fork.c`'s version.
+
+### 4. vma_is_shared_maywrite() doesn't exist in 6.6
+**Conflict**: Patch uses `vma_is_shared_maywrite()`. 6.6 doesn't have it.
+**Resolution**: Used `vm_flags & VM_SHARED` instead (same as patch 0025 adaptation).
+
+### 5. collect_procs_pfn doesn't exist in 6.6
+**Conflict**: Patch modifies `collect_procs_pfn` in `mm/memory-failure.c`.
+**Resolution**: Function doesn't exist in 6.6; skipped.
+
+### 6. call_action_complete doesn't exist in 6.6
+**Conflict**: Patch modifies `call_action_complete` in `mm/vma.c`.
+**Resolution**: Function doesn't exist in 6.6; skipped.
+
+### 7. i_mmap_vma_nid forward declaration needed
+**Conflict**: `unlink_file_vma_batch_same_key` uses `i_mmap_vma_nid` before its definition.
+**Resolution**: Added forward declaration `static int i_mmap_vma_nid(struct vm_area_struct *vma);` before the batch functions.
+
+### 8. __remove_shared_vm_struct signature
+**Conflict**: In 7.0-rc1, `__remove_shared_vm_struct` is in `mm/vma.c` and uses `i_mmap_remove_vma`. In 6.6, it's in `mm/mmap.c`.
+**Resolution**: Modified 6.6's `__remove_shared_vm_struct` to call `i_mmap_remove_vma`.
+
+## Risk Analysis
+
+| Risk | Level | Mitigation |
+|------|-------|------------|
+| Config defaults off - no runtime impact unless enabled | Low | `default n` in Kconfig |
+| DAX/hugetlb excluded from sharding | Low | Explicit checks in `i_mmap_can_shard()` |
+| Shard migration under write lock | Medium | One-time migration; small mappings only |
+| Debugfs stats memory | Low | Fixed-size array, only under CONFIG_DEBUG_FS |
+| Inline stub overhead when disabled | Low | All stubs inline to legacy path |
+
+## Test Results
+- **Compile**: Passed (core kernel/ and mm/ build cleanly; driver errors are pre-existing)
+- **test-kernel**: Passed — VM boots successfully with 4 CPUs, 2 NUMA nodes
+
+## Verification Commands
+```bash
+make -j$(nproc) kernel/ mm/  # builds cleanly
+# QEMU boots with 4 CPUs, 2 NUMA nodes
+# uname -r: 6.6.0-...-dirty
+```
